"EmoBench-Reddit: A Hierarchical Benchmark for Evaluating the Emotional Intelligence of Multimodal Large Language Models (https://arxiv.org/html/2509.11101v1)\nciteturn3187view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn3184view1\",\"lineno\":230}); Total lines: 356\nL199: ### 4.2 Evaluation Strategies\nL200: \nL201: To deeply investigate model behaviors, we designed two evaluation strategies:\nL202: \nL203:   1. 1.\nL204: \nL205: Gated Evaluation: In this strategy, we first evaluate the model on all perception tasks. We only proceed to evaluate the cognition tasks for a given data point if the model’s average accuracy on the perception tasks for that item is above 75%. This strategy aims to test the hypothesis that accurate visual perception is a prerequisite for effective cognitive reasoning.\nL206: \nL207:   2. 2.\nL208: Contextual Evaluation: Here, we simulate a continuous conversation. When asking each new question, we provide the history of previous questions and the model’s answers as context. This strategy tests whether the model can effectively use conversational context to refine its understanding and improve accuracy on subsequent questions.\nL209: \nL210: The results in this paper are primarily based on the \"Gated Evaluation\" strategy, as it more clearly reveals the dependency between perception and cognition.\nL211: ## 5 Experimental Setup\nL212: \nL213: ### 5.1 Models Evaluated\nL214: \nL215: We selected 9 representative MLLMs from industry and academia, covering different organizations, technical approaches, and parameter scales:\nL216: \nL217:   * •\nL218: \nL219: OpenAI Series: GPT-5, GPT-4o, GPT-4V\nL220: \nL221:   * •\nL222: \nL223: Google Series: Gemini-2.5-pro, Gemini-2.0-flash\nL224: \nL225:   * •\nL226: \nL227: Chinese Models: GLM-4v-plus (Zhipu AI), Qwen-vl-max, Qwen-vl-7b (Alibaba)\nL228: \nL229:   * •\nL230: \nL231: Other Open-Source Models: Deepseek-vl-7b\nL232: ### 5.2 Experimental Environment\nL233: \nL234: All closed-source models were accessed via their official APIs. We used a uniform, concise instruction format for all models to ensure fairness and avoid prompt engineering bias. All experiments were conducted in a zero-shot setting.\nL235: ## 6 Results and Analysis\nL236: \nL237: We conducted a comprehensive evaluation of the 9 models on EmoBench-Reddit. The results are shown in Table cite45†1 .\nL238: Emotion  | Task  | gpt-4o  | gpt-4V  | gpt-5  | glm-4v-plus  | qwen-vl-max  | gemini-2.0-flash  | gemini-2.5-pro  | qwen-vl-7b  | Deepseek-vl-7b\nL239: --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nL240: Sad  | Perception 1  | 0.90  | 0.90  | 0.97  | 0.85  | 0.92  | 0.87  | 0.92  | 0.87  | 0.75\nL241: Perception 2(a)  | 0.85  | 0.77  | 0.88  | 0.92  | 0.77  | 0.87  | 0.92  | 0.72  | 0.57\nL242: Perception 2(b)  | 0.68  | 0.66  | 0.93  | 0.84  | 0.75  | 0.79  | 0.88  | 0.89  | 0.50\nL243: Perception 3  | 0.63  | 0.72  | 0.72  | 0.58  | 0.73  | 0.70  | 0.75  | 0.73  | 0.43\nL244: Cognition 1  | 0.76  | 0.80  | 0.82  | 0.78  | 0.73  | 0.76  | 0.87  | 0.71  | 0.67\nL245: Cognition 2  | 0.71  | 0.73  | 0.71  | 0.71  | 0.56  | 0.71  | 0.69  | 0.54  | 0.46\nL246: Cognition 3  | 0.60  | 0.62  | 0.64  | 0.76  | 0.59  | 0.47  | 0.67  | 0.50  | 0.50\nL247: Humor  | Perception 1  | 0.90  | 0.84  | 0.88  | 0.95  | 0.90  | 0.92  | 0.96  | 0.92  | 0.90\nL248: Perception 2(a)  | 0.88  | 0.80  | 0.89  | 0.84  | 0.87  | 0.89  | 0.95  | 0.89  | 0.76\nL249: Perception 2(b)  | 0.73  | 0.80  | 0.66  | 0.88  | 0.86  | 0.88  | 0.84  | 0.88  | 0.78\nL250: Perception 3  | 0.71  | 0.77  | 0.76  | 0.78  | 0.73  | 0.78  | 0.76  | 0.78  | 0.53\nL251: Cognition 1  | 0.88  | 0.77  | 0.84  | 0.80  | 0.77  | 0.76  | 0.88  | 0.76  | 0.78\nL252: Cognition 2  | 0.66  | 0.62  | 0.81  | 0.61  | 0.66  | 0.66  | 0.63  | 0.66  | 0.71\nL253: Cognition 3  | 0.81  | 0.71  | 0.81  | 0.69  | 0.73  | 0.69  | 0.85  | 0.69  | 0.58\n--------------------------------------